<item>
<title>Sudan's civil war: the situation</title>
<link>https://map.igred.org/crisis/sudan/</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">igred-summary-sudan-2026-10-20T18:34:55.161Z</guid>
<pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 18:34:55 GMT</pubDate>
<description>&lt;p&gt;The Sudanese army is conducting drone strikes on civilian sites, including a market in Abyei where more than 150 people were killed, a mourners' gathering and a fuel market where over 300 were killed, and a market in southern Sudan with hundreds of casualties. The Rapid Support Forces are also using drones to hit economic targets such as gold-mining areas in West Kordofan and near the Egypt border, causing dozens of civilian deaths. These attacks extend drone use from combatant targets to markets, mourners and economic sites, expanding civilian exposure to aerial strikes. 4,680 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261020-more-than-150-killed-sudan-drone-strike-disputed-abyei-border-region&quot;&gt;France 24&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/19/us-migrants-deportation-ukraine-sudan&quot;&gt;The Guardian&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.un.org/feed/view/en/story/2026/10/1168612&quot;&gt;UN News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;DW.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiWkFVX3lxTE1wczhTM2FMeGJjMDRDbnROVkI0YVFUQmhlOWRyOFBGOXdPbFpLdlo2LWVqLUZERFF2blFrMVIwMkVuTG9Ca2Zmb2dRUGhQUmdxSWhfUzBQbE9GUQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;BBC&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Hindu&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiXkFVX3lxTE5faHFBVmNRRW1tb0tMRWN0MThmT1JESFNaNDRJaTVMUkhwRHFXOTQ5T29jaDVtdDJvWXA0UHl4MU9YWTUweDVuS0FQRkZWLWE4SGQ5Zy1KWnZFdjVHRWc?oc=5&quot;&gt;BBC&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
</item>
